1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * From [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Altun_Jan_Khatun '''Wikipedia'''], the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Altun Jan Khatun''' (died 1060; meaning "Golden soul") was the Empress of the Seljuk Empire as the first wife and chief consort of Tughril, the founder of the Seljuk Empire, ruling from 1037 to 1063.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Early life=
2 CONT
2 CONT Altun Jan Khatun was a Turkish woman, possibly from Khwarezm. Before becoming Tughril Beg's wife she had been married to the Khwarezm Shah. Her son by that marriage, Anoushiravan, apparently remained with her after she married Tug
2 CONC hril Beg.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Toghril Beg is reported to have consulted his chief wife Altun Jan in affairs, Sibt ibn al-Jawzi states that she was a religious woman, much given to charitable works, of good judgement and firm determination.[2][3] When Tughril B
2 CONC eg went to Hamadan in 1058 to deal with the revolt of Ibrahim Inal, he sent Altun Jan, Anoushiravan and al-Kunduri to Baghdad. Al-Kunduri appears on this occasion to have considered replacing Tughril Bey by Anoushiravan. Anoushira
2 CONC van rebelled but was captured. He was imprisoned in Rey and was killed after Tughril's death.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Death and aftermath=
2 CONT
2 CONT She died of edema in 1059 in Zanjan. Tughril grieved for her greatly, and her bier was carried to Rey, where she was buried.[5][6] She held estates in Iran. Just before her death she bequeathed her states, assignments and pensions
2 CONC  to the Caliph's daughter. Tughril assigned these to the latter when the marriage contract between him and the caliph's daughter was finally concluded in 1062.[7] According to some sources it was her who requested Tughril to marry
2 CONC  the caliph's daughter at her deathbed.
2 CONT
