1 NAME Ayşe Hatun /of Smyrna/
2 GIVN Ayşe Hatun
2 _MARNM of Smyrna
1 SEX F
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kilij_Arslan_I '''Wikipedia page'''] of her first husband, Kilij Arslan:
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the death of Malik Shah I the individual tribes, the Danishmends, Mangujekids, Saltuqids, Chaka, Tengribirmish begs, Artuqids (Ortoqids) and Akhlat-Shahs, had started vying with each other to establish their own independ
2 CONC ent states. Alexius Comnenus's Byzantine intrigues further complicated the situation. He married the daughter of the Emir of the Chaka to attempt to ally himself against the Byzantines, who commanded a strong naval fleet. In 1094,
2 CONC  Kilij Arslan received a letter from Alexius suggesting that the Chaka sought to target him to move onto the Byzantines, thereupon Kilij Arslan marched with an army to Smyrna, Chaka’s capital, and invited his father-in-law to a ba
2 CONC nquet in his tent where he slew him while he was intoxicated.
2 CONT
2 CONT * from the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belek_Ghazi '''Wikipedia page'''] of her second husband, Belek Ghazi:
2 CONT
2 CONT Next year he married to Ayşe Hatun, widow of the late Anatolian Seljuk sultan Kılıç Arslan I . By this prestigious marriage, he formed family ties with the Seljuk family.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT =References=
2 CONT
2 CONT * [2] [http://www.nkfu.com/belek-balak-gazi-hayati/ '''Belek Gazi'''] (source in Turkish)
