2 CONT '''Malik-Shah III''' (died 1160[1]) ruled as Sultan of Great Seljuq from 1152-53. He was the son of Mahmud II of Great Seljuq. In 1153, he was deposed and was succeeded by his brother, Muhammad. Following his death in 1160, his so
2 CONC n Mahmud was held in Istakhr by the Salghurids as a rival claimant to the Seljuq throne.[2]
