1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rustam_Dushmanziyar '''Wikipedia'''], the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Rustam Dushmanziyar''' (Persian: رستم دشمنزار‎) was a Dailamite aristocrat and the ancestor of the Kakuyid dynasty. His real name was Rustam but was known as Dushmanziyar, which is the Arabized version of ''Dushmanzar'', meanin
2 CONC g "he who brings grief to his enemy".
2 CONT
2 CONT =Biography=
2 CONT
2 CONT Rustam was the brother of the wife of the Buyid ruler Fakhr al-Dawla, Sayyida Shirin,[1][2] who was sister, or most likely, the niece of the Bavandid ruler Al-Marzuban.[3] Rustam also had a son named Muhammad ibn Rustam Dushmanziy
2 CONC ar, who would later establish the Kakuyid dynasty of Isfahan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rustam, because of his great service to Fakhr al-Dawla, he was rewarded with land in Alborz in appreciation of his services. His duty was to protect Ray and northern Jibal against the local leaders from Tabaristan.[4] Rustam later
2 CONC  died at an unknown date before 1007, which was the date Muhammad ibn Rustam Dushmanziyar established the Kakuyid dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT =References=
2 CONT
2 CONT # Huart 1993, p. 667-668.
2 CONT # Kennedy 2004, p. 244.
2 CONT # Madelung 1975, p. 217.
2 CONT # Bosworth 1984, p. 773-774.
2 CONT
