1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_IV_of_Georgia
2 CONT
2 CONT Giorgi IV Lasha (Lasha Giorgi; in Georgian: გიორგი IV ლაშა, ლაშა გიორგი) (1191-1223) from the House of Bagrationi, was king of Georgia from 1213 to 1223.
2 CONT
2 CONT A son of Queen Tamar and David Soslani, he was declared as a coregent by his mother in 1207. He continued Tamar’s policy of strengthening of the Georgia feudal state. He put down the revolts in neighbouring Muslim vassal states in
2 CONC  the 1210s and began preparations for a large-scale campaign against Jerusalem to support the Crusaders in 1220. However, the Mongol approach to the Georgian borders made the Crusade plan unrealizable. The first Mongol defeated tw
2 CONC o Georgian armies in 1221-1222 and left Inner Caucasus. However, Georgians suffered heavy losses in this war and the King himself was severely wounded. As a result Lasha Giorgi became severely ill and died at the age of 31. He was
2 CONC  succeeded by his sister Rusudan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Giorgi Lasha was known as a free minded person and met much criticism from a conservative feudal society. The nobles and Christian clergymen rejected and failed to recognize his wife, a girl from a non-noble family. Ultimately, th
2 CONC e King had to compromise and divorced her, refusing, however, to marry anyone else.
2 CONT
2 CONT Medieval sources are presently the best available sources. They characterize Giorgi IV as a wise ruler and brave warrior, while others point to his immoral life style and addiction to mysticism and even Sufism.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was survived by a son David (the future King David VII Ulu)
