2 CONT ==Isaac Komnenos (brother of Alexios I)==
2 CONT Isaac Komnenos or Comnenus (Greek: Ἰσαάκιος Κομνηνός, ca. 1050 – 1102/1104) was a notable Byzantine general in the 1070s and one of the major supporters of Byzantine Emperor Alexios I Komnenos (r. 1081–1118), who was his younger b
2 CONC rother. Alexios created the title of sebastokrator for Isaac.
2 CONT
2 CONT By his wife Irene, he had several children:[3][4][5]
2 CONT
2 CONT #John Komnenos, protosebastos and governor (doux) of Dyrrhachium from 1092 to 1105/6
2 CONT #Alexios Komnenos, pansebastos and doux of Dyrrhachium after 1105/6
2 CONT #Constantine Komnenos, pansebastos and doux of Beroea, later megas droungarios
2 CONT #Adrianos Komnenos, became a monk, later Archbishop of Bulgaria as John IV
2 CONT #Sophia Komnene, married Nikephoros Dokeianos
2 CONT #Eudokia Komnene, married Nikephoros Botaneiates
2 CONT #Two unnamed daughters, one of them was engaged to Gregory Gabras
2 CONT #''The second unnamed daughter PERHAPS Barbara, 3rd wife of Svyatopolk II Mikhail Iziaslavich (Note from FARKAS Mihály László)''
2 CONT
