1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahmud_of_Ghazni '''Wikipedia'''], the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Yamīn-ud-Dawla Abul-Qāṣim Maḥmūd ibn Sebüktegīn''' (Persian: یمین‌الدوله ابوالقاسم محمود بن سبکتگین‎), more commonly known as '''Mahmud of Ghazni''' (محمود غزنوی;‎ 2 November 971 CE – 30 April 1030 CE), also known as '''Mahmūd-
2 CONC i Zābulī''' (محمود زابلی), was the most prominent ruler of the Ghaznavid Empire. He conquered the eastern Iranian lands and the northwestern Indian subcontinent (modern Afghanistan and Pakistan) from 997 to his death in 1030. Mahm
2 CONC ud turned the former provincial city of Ghazna into the wealthy capital of an extensive empire which covered most of today's Afghanistan, eastern Iran, and Pakistan, by looting the riches and wealth from the then Indian subcontine
2 CONC nt.[2][3] He was the first ruler to carry the title Sultan ("authority"), signifying the extent of his power, though preserving the ideological link to the suzerainty of the Abbassid Caliphate. During his rule, he invaded and plun
2 CONC dered parts of Hindustan (east of the Indus River) 17 times.[3]
2 CONT
