1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ismail_of_Ghazni '''Wikipedia'''], the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ismail of Ghazni''' (Persian: اسماعیل غزنوی‎) was the emir of Ghazna from 997 until 998. He succeeded his father emir Sabuktigin, who died of an illness acquired in Balkh during a campaign in the Samanid civil war. Ismail was d
2 CONC esignated his successor by Sabuktigin on his death-bed, while Mahmud, the older brother who was involved in the Samanid civil war, was stationed in Nishapur.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon receiving these news Mahmud of Ghazni contested Ismail's right to the throne and divested his charge of Nishapur to his uncle Borghuz and younger brother Nur-ud-Din Yusuf and marched upon Ghazna in what is now Afghanistan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mahmud won the Battle of Ghazni and took the crown from Ismail. Ismail spent the rest of his life confined to a fort in Guzgan. Historians have extrapolated that Sabuktigin chose Ismail because his other two sons both had a slave 
2 CONC as mother, from Ferdowsi's later satirization of Mahmud for being descended from slaves on both maternal and paternal side.
2 CONT
