2 CONT * From the [http://www.iranicaonline.org/articles/qotlogh-tarkan-khatun '''Encyclopaedia Iranica'''] page of Qotlog Tarkan Khatun:
2 CONT
2 CONT QOTLOḠ TARKĀN ḴĀTUN (or Tarkan), ʿEṢMAT-AL-DONYĀ WA’L-DIN, Qara Ḵetāy ruler of Kerman (655-89/1257-83).  She probably was born between 605-610/1208-1213 in Transoxania; she was enslaved during childhood and acquired by an old merc
2 CONC hant from Isfahan, who raised her as his own daughter and provided her with an excellent education (Anonymous, p. 96).  Other historians first mention Tarkān as a concubine of Ḡiāt̠-al-Din Piršāh, a son of Sultan Moḥammad Ḵˇāraz
2 CONC mšāh (Waṣṣāf, 1853, p. 287; for the name Tarkān/Tarkan, see Qazvini, pp. 62-63), and subsequently Borāq Ḥājeb, a chamberlain (ḥājeb) in Sultan Moḥammad’s service and the first Qotloḡḵāniya ruler of Kerman (Mostawfi, p. 530).
2 CONC   Four months after Borāq’s death (20 Ḏu’l-ḥejja 632/5 September 1235), his nephew and successor, Qoṭb-al-Din Moḥammad, married Tarkān. 
