2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daylamites
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mu%27izz_al-Dawla
2 CONT '''Ahmad ibn Buya''' also known as '''Mu'izz al-Dawla "Fortifier of the Dynasty"'''
2 CONT "Fortifier of the Dynasty"), was the first of the Buyid emirs of Iraq, ruling from 945 until his death.
2 CONT Ahmad was the son of Buya, a Daylamite fisherman from Lahijan,[1] who had left his Zoroastrian faith and converted to Islam.[2] Ahmad had two older brothers named 'Ali and Hasan, and a sister named Kama.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Ahmad son of Buya of Daylam - Military officer for Makan, Samanid gov. of Rayy
2 CONT
2 CONT Hasan was the son of Buya, a Dailamite fisherman from Lahijan, who left his Zoroastrian faith and converted to Islam. Hasan had an older brother named 'Ali and a younger brother named Ahmad. He also had a sister named Kama.
2 CONT
2 CONT In around 928, Hasan's brother 'Ali joined the services of Makan, who was the Samanid governor of Ray. 'Ali then managed to gain military positions for Hasan and their other brother Ahmad. At the time, Hasan was about thirty years
2 CONC  old. When Makan attacked his Samanid overlords and was subsequently defeated by the Ziyarid prince Mardavij, the brothers transferred their allegiance to the latter.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the following years, 'Ali repudiated his subservience to Mardavij and, after some time, managed to create an empire in Fars.
