1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Marija de Katchen Sewaday==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sahakanuysh
2 CONT
2 CONT Sahakanuysh (Armenian: Սահականույշ, 10th century) was the third Queen of the Bagratid Kingdom and member of Aranshahik Dynasty. She was the wife of the third Bagratuni king - Ashot the Iron (914-928).
2 CONT
2 CONT Sahakanuysh was the daughter of Prince of Gardman Sahak Sevada. She had two brothers - Grigor the Great, prince of Khachen (Nagorno-Karabakh Republic), and Hovhannes-Senekerim, prince of Parisos. The latter was situated in Utik pr
2 CONC ovince of Armenia (nowadays - Azerbaijan). Her sister Shahandukht married to Smbat Syuni, and became the first queen of Syunik kingdom.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ashot the Iron and Sahakanuysh had no children.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marie_de_Katchen
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie de Katchen (en arménien : Սահականույշ) est la troisième reine (consort) bagratide d'Arménie. Elle épouse le roi Achot II d'Arménie en 917, qui règne entre les années 914 et 928.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie de Katchen était la fille du prince de Gardman Sahak Sevada. Elle avait deux frères - Grigor le Grand, prince de Khatchen (Nagorno-Karabakh), et Hovhannes-Senekerim, prince de Parisos. Ce dernier était situé dans la province
2 CONC  de Outik en Arménie (aujourd'hui - Azerbaïdjan). Sa sœur Shahandukht est marié à Smbat Ier de Syunik, et est devenue la première reine du Royaume de Syunik.
2 CONT
2 CONT Selon Christian Settipani, Achot d'Arménie et Marie de Katchen seraient les parents de Rhipsime, épouse de Nikola Kumet, eux-mêmes parents de Samuel de Bulgarie. [https://books.google.com/books?redir_esc=y&id=IVdoAAAAMAAJ&focus=se
2 CONC archwithinvolume&q=Rhipsime link] Comment: doesn’t seem to say that.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ARMENIA.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT b)         ASHOT Bagratuni (-[928]).  The De Administrando Imperio of Konstantinos Porphyrogenetos names "Asotium…et Apasacium" as the two sons of "Symbatii…principum principis"[61].  The Histoire of Jean VI Catholicos records tha
2 CONC t "le chef des eunuques…[de] Afschin" took "Aschod le fils du roi" and "la femme de Mouschegh, frère d´Aschod", who had been captured "dans la forteresse de Kars", and returned them to King Smbat[62].  Kirakos Ganjaketsi's History
2 CONC  of Armenia records that "his son Ashot" succeeded after the death of "Smbat Bagratuni" and ruled "at the order of Emperor Romanus for eight years"[63].  Defeated by Yusuf ostikan of Azerbaijan, he was crowned in 914 as ASHOT II K
2 CONC ing of Armenia by Adarnase II King of Iberia.  The Histoire of Jean VI Catholicos records that "Aschod fils de Sempad" was made king "par le roi des Ibériens"[64].  After visiting Constantinople, he returned to Armenia with Byzant
2 CONC ine forces to fight ostikan Yusuf and his cousin Ashot, whom Yusuf had installed as anti-king of Armenia[65].  After Yusuf's fall and recall to Baghdad in 919, King Ashot was granted the title Shahanshah [King of Kings].  m ([917]
2 CONC ) MARIE of Kachen, daughter of SAHAK Sevata & his wife ---.  The Histoire of Jean VI Catholicos records that "le roi Aschod, fils de roi" married "la fille du grand ischkhan Isaac [Sahak] surnommé Sévata", dated to [917] from the 
2 CONC context[66]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT * * https://www.geni.com/people/Ripsimia/6000000002187821458 is NOT a known child  
2 CONT * A Genealogy Report For HAROLD FLOYD CAULK [http://dl.vdocuments.site/download/6ff9f7f468894f043d8f06a0e31cfb2afcefcff26237a8769a2ca7f24da3134ec64f0ec9d10feeeebe656256393c9b3cf332d8600885ee996031066001916ea63rPRFIW%2Fi4TgMXKMaJx8
2 CONC cBfNb2%2FjSSXSHUDaCUDZt6Lyz8SdgrvKJn9eEaC0Zq6zlZfLkDdGz8ZpIfLsQEJSWFuMqhFXFSlErTWOBRosPP4%3D link to download]
2 CONT *comm. 59 [http://www.vostlit.info/Texts/rus/Drash/primtext5.phtml archive] “ 59 . Sahak - Sahak Sevada, one of the sons of the king of the Eastern borders of Armenia, or Alvank - Hamam-Grigor (see: note 11 to chap. XXXIII). Armen
2 CONC ian historian mov. Feces. in his History of the country, Alvank writes about him: “... Sahak, nicknamed Sevada, a brave and skillful husband, conquered the area of ​​Gardman, Kosti-i Parn; he subjugated the robber chieftains of Dz
2 CONC oraget » (p. 278-279). Sahak Sevada was bound by ties of kinship with the royal house of Bagratunn and the Ishkhan of Syunik: one of his daughters later became the wife of Ashot II Erkat, and the second - the wife of Smbat, the wa
2 CONC sher of Ishkhan Syunik. Sevada was an enlightened man and contributed in every way to the development of literature and the spread of education. As Mov writes . Feces. (p. 279):“He loved literature and established a school in his 
2 CONC house.” (See about him: Ulubabyan B. Principality of Khachen, pp. 81, 103-106).” “ 4 . The coronation of Ashot II Erkat is dated to 914.”
