1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Bagrat I King of Abkhazia''' from 887–898/899 Preceded by Adarnase Shavliani, Succeeded by Constantine I http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bagrat_I_of_Abkhazia
2 CONT
2 CONT Bagrat I (Georgian: ბაგრატ I) was the King of Abkhazia between 887/88 and 898/99. He was the son of Demetrius II of the Anosids dynasty. After the usurper John Shavliani seized the throne Bagrat fled to Constantinople and lived th
2 CONC ere for some time until he returned to Abkhazia in 887/888, deposed and put to death Adarnase Shavliani (the son of John Shavliani) and reclaimed the throne. He was married to the daughter of Guaram Bagrationi, the ruler of Tao-Kl
2 CONC ardjeti and had a son Constantine who succeeded him to the throne of Abkhazia.
2 CONT
2 CONT See also
2 CONT
2 CONT Abkhazian Kingdom Divan of the Abkhazian Kings
2 CONT
