1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Second marriage==
2 CONT
2 CONT Demetrius' second wife was the Mongol woman Solghar, by whom he had two sons, Baidu and Yadgar, and a daughter, Jigda.[7] Following the death of Demetrius, she retired from Georgia, bringing Baidu and Yadgar with her to her father
2 CONC 's home in "Tartary".[5] Baidu then reappears in the Georgian annals as an envoy of his half-brother David VIII to the khan of the Golden Horde, Toqta, in 1298.[9] According to one genealogical hypothesis, Jigda is the same as Jia
2 CONC jak, the second wife of the emepror Alexios II of Trebizond.[1] However, Jiajak was more likely a member of the Jaqeli family.
