2 CONT His son Mehmed Bey took over the family possessions around Sinop and pursued a prudent policy of allegiance to the Mongols, which was also pursued under his son Mesud Bey's period as Bey. Mesud Bey was kidnapped by the Genoese in 
2 CONC 1298 and was held for a heavy ransom. The last representative of the Pervane's line was probably the Gazi Chelebi, a notable pirate who ruled Sinop in the first decades of the 14th century.
