1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Izz_al-Dawla
2 CONT Izz al-Dawla was born as Bakhtiyar, and was the son of Mu'izz al-Dawla. He also had three brothers named Sanad al-Dawla, Marzuban and Abu Ishaq Ibrahim. Bakhtiyar, during his early life, married a daughter of the Dailamite officer
2 CONC  Lashkarwarz.  
2 CONT
2 CONT also known as 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rukn_al-Dawla
2 CONT Rāfiʿ ibn Abīʾl-Layl ibn ʿUlayyān al-Kalbī (Arabic: رافع بن أبي ليلى بن عليان الكلبي) (fl. 1028–1038), also known by his laqab (honorific epithet) ʿIzz al-Dawla (Arabic: عزالدولة), was the emir of the Kalb tribe of Syria in the mi
2 CONC d-11th century.[1]
